-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party material included in this source tree
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/sku_table.rs
  The table of LAN-capable Govee models and their segment counts is derived
  from the device capability table in govee-local-api
  (https://github.com/Galorhallen/govee-local-api), Copyright Galorhallen,
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  Modifications: the data was converted from Python to a Rust constant table,
  reduced to the RGB, colour-temperature and segment-count fields, and is
  consumed by ReadySetGlow's own device logic.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Protocol references (no code copied)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ReadySetGlow's implementation of the Govee LAN protocol was written from public
descriptions of how the protocol works. No source code from the following
projects is included:

  * OpenRGB (https://gitlab.com/CalcProgrammer1/OpenRGB): description of the
    "razer" per-LED streaming packet format.
  * Community reverse-engineering notes on the Govee BLE packet format
    (https://notes.generalzero.org/Reverse%20Engineering/Signals/Bluetooth/Govee_lights.html).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Binary distributions
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Compiled builds of ReadySetGlow statically include Rust crates from crates.io, each
under its own licence (predominantly MIT and/or Apache-2.0). They include:

  * egui / eframe / epaint (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
  * cpal (Apache-2.0)
  * rustfft, socket2, serde, serde_json, base64, directories
    (MIT and/or Apache-2.0)

Builds also embed the default egui fonts:

  * Ubuntu Light: Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0
  * Noto Emoji: SIL Open Font License 1.1
  * Hack: MIT License, Copyright 2018 Source Foundry Authors; contains
    Bitstream Vera material under the Bitstream Vera License
  * emoji-icon-font: MIT License, Copyright (c) 2014 John Slegers

A full list of dependencies with their licence texts can be generated with
cargo-about (https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about) and should
accompany any binary release.

